---
import {officeBase,gmailGuideUrl,gmailPrompts,mailLabels,officialSources} from '../../data/workflow-en/gmail';
import CaseBoundaries from '../CaseBoundaries.astro';
import CaseVerification from '../CaseVerification.astro';
import WorkflowPrompt from '../preview/WorkflowPrompt.astro';
import GmailPractice from './GmailPractice.astro';
const toc=[['result','Inputs and complete outputs'],['prepare','Preparation and capabilities'],['automation-boundaries','Execution and takeover boundaries'],['rules','01 Define label rules'],['practice','02 Practice with synthetic emails'],['read-only','03 Read a small real batch'],['write','04 Validate labels and drafts separately'],['repeat','05 Save a Skill, then review a Routine'],['troubleshoot','Troubleshooting and acceptance'],['downloads','Download practice files'],['sources','Sources and verification scope']];
const problems=[
 ['Connected, but messages cannot be read','Check account, query and actual tools. For Workspace, inspect administrator policies. Do not repeatedly retry or change login paths to widen access.'],
 ['Unpaid bills and paid receipts are mixed','Check explicit transaction status. Compare M03/M04, revise the rule and rerun the sample.'],
 ['An email matches several categories','Use one primary label for this workflow and Review for insufficient context. Preserve all existing unrelated labels.'],
 ['The same email has duplicate drafts','Pause creation and compare original message_id with recorded draft_id. A timeout does not prove no draft was created; inspect before retrying.'],
 ['A new reply in an old thread was skipped','Deduplicate by individual message_id, not thread_id alone. Old labels do not automatically classify new replies.'],
 ['The body is truncated or an attachment is essential','Use Review and state coverage. Attachments are excluded by default; define a separate file scope if needed.'],
 ['Draft creation is unavailable','Return reply text marked not saved to Gmail. A page preview is not proof of a saved draft.'],
 ['More messages exist than the run limit','Retain an overflow queue and known remaining count, or say the remainder is unknown. A truncated batch is not all email.'],
 ['No Routine brief arrived','Check execution state, Bot, time zone and next run. Distinguish no new content from connection failure; validate manually before resuming.'],
];
const checks=['All 8 sample emails have an outcome and counts total 8; M06 remains Review.','M03 is an unpaid bill; M04 is a paid receipt.','Only M01/M08 have sample drafts; unknown price, delivery date and meeting time remain unconfirmed.','The real trial can be traced to account, query,original message_id and operation result.','A repeat small batch creates no duplicate drafts; failures and partial success identify a stopping point.','Sent has no new messages; inbox membership,old labels and read state did not change unexpectedly.'];
---
<div id="main" class="wf-shell">
 <nav class="wf-breadcrumb" data-pagefind-ignore aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={officeBase}>Office & information</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Complete Gmail tutorial</span></nav>
 <header class="wf-guide-hero"><div class="wf-kicker">IN-DEPTH TUTORIAL / 01</div><h1>Gmail inbox organization:<br/>labels, drafts and a daily brief</h1><p class="wf-lead">Classify eight sample emails before reading a small batch of your own. Every stage includes a prompt, deliverable and acceptance check. Consider recurring runs after manual validation.</p><div class="wf-guide-meta"><span>Prepared by shancha</span><span>Build your first email workflow</span><span>6 labels + Review</span></div><div class="wf-actions"><a class="wf-button" href="#result">Explore the complete example ↓</a><a class="wf-text-link" href="#downloads">Download practice files ↗</a></div></header>
 <details class="wf-mobile-toc" data-pagefind-ignore><summary>On this page</summary><ol>{toc.map(([id,title])=><li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}</ol></details>
 <div class="wf-guide-grid"><article class="wf-prose">
  <section id="result"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>THE RESULT</span><h2 id="result-heading">From original emails to today’s action list</h2></div><p>Keep three deliverables: a traceable classification table, reply drafts for review and a one-page brief of actions and exceptions. Switch tabs below to inspect the complete input and reference outputs.</p><div class="wf-scope"><strong>Demonstration scope</strong><p>The practice uses original synthetic material. Tabs only switch page content. Real Gmail connections, label writes, saved drafts and Routine execution remain untested. Start by giving the files to a Bot.</p></div><GmailPractice/></section>
  <section id="prepare"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>BEFORE YOU START</span><h2 id="prepare-heading">Prepare the sample exercise and real account separately</h2></div><div class="wf-two-cards"><div><h3>Practice without an inbox</h3><ul><li>Download <code>source-mails.json</code> and <code>label-rules.md</code>.</li><li>Upload them to a Bot conversation; use only these files at this stage.</li><li>Compare the reference afterward and refine disagreements into rules.</li></ul></div><div><h3>Connect your own mailbox later</h3><ul><li>Add an available Gmail connector through Connect apps and complete authorization yourself.</li><li>Verify account, actual tools and visible scope; capabilities vary by environment.</li><li>Start read-only with at most 10 messages in a defined query; review writes separately.</li></ul></div></div><p>The source documentation describes connector installation through Connect apps. Connector accounts and cloud-computer sessions can be shared across Bots within an account; a Bot name or a prompt saying read-only does not establish permission isolation. <a class="wf-source-ref" href={officialSources[0].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connection reference ↗</a></p><WorkflowPrompt id="gmail-capability" text={gmailPrompts.capability} title="Preparation · Check Gmail connection and tools"/><div class="wf-check"><b>Acceptance check</b><p>Get an actual available/unavailable tool list. If tools only read, retain classifications and reply text as files for manual labels and drafts.</p></div></section>
  <CaseBoundaries slug="gmail-inbox-triage" english />
			<section id="rules" class="wf-stage"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>STEP 01</span><h2 id="rules-heading">Agree classification rules before processing</h2></div><p>Use six business labels plus <code>Review</code>. Prefix real workflow labels with <code>GBG/</code> so they are identifiable while preserving existing labels.</p><div class="wf-label-grid">{mailLabels.map(label=><div><span class="wf-tag">{label.name}</span><h3>{label.zh}</h3><p>{label.rule}</p></div>)}</div><div class="wf-note"><strong>Resolve overlaps in this order</strong><p>Missing key context → Review; explicit paid receipt → Receipts; unresolved money → Money; then Action, Waiting, Newsletters, Keep. This is the exercise’s business convention; Gmail allows multiple labels.</p></div><p>Apply workflow business labels to original received messages, not drafts. Drafts have separate identity and state. <a class="wf-source-ref" href={officialSources[5].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gmail label reference ↗</a></p><div class="wf-check"><b>Acceptance check</b><p>Explain why M03 is Money, M04 Receipts and M06 Review before moving on.</p></div></section>
  <section id="practice" class="wf-stage"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>STEP 02</span><h2 id="practice-heading">Calibrate with eight synthetic emails</h2></div><p>Upload input and rules without the reference answer. Let the Bot classify independently, then return to Labels and drafts to compare. M01–M08 are practice ids; real runs need actual message_id values.</p><WorkflowPrompt id="gmail-classify" text={gmailPrompts.classify} title="Practice · Classify uploaded samples only"/><div class="wf-check"><b>Expected output</b><p>Eight rows: Action 2 and one each in the other six categories, with source evidence and next steps. These answers calibrate this rule set; they do not measure real inbox accuracy.</p></div><p>You may choose a different business rule, such as payment reminders under Action. Update the reference table, draft policy and brief counts together, then rerun the same input.</p></section>
  <section id="read-only" class="wf-stage"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>STEP 03</span><h2 id="read-only-heading">Read only a small batch from your real inbox</h2></div><p>Specify your account and a query such as <code>in:inbox newer_than:2d</code>, capped at 10 messages. Search may display conversations; check each message’s received time and identity before counting. <a class="wf-source-ref" href={officialSources[4].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gmail search reference ↗</a></p><div class="wf-note"><strong>Three identifiers you will need</strong><p><code>message_id</code> identifies an original message, <code>thread_id</code> a conversation and <code>draft_id</code> a saved draft. Return these identifiers for audit and deduplication. Synthetic M ids cannot be substituted into a real account.</p></div><WorkflowPrompt id="gmail-read" text={gmailPrompts.readOnly} title="Connection · Read-only classification of a specified scope"/><div class="wf-check"><b>Acceptance check</b><p>Find every original in Gmail and inspect evidence, count and gaps. Stop at read-only output if stable ids, full bodies or account scope are unclear.</p></div></section>
  <section id="write" class="wf-stage"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>STEP 04</span><h2 id="write-heading">Validate labels and saved drafts separately</h2></div><p>Select 3 originals from the reviewed list and name exact message_id values and actions. Approval covers that trial. If tool-level controls exist, disable sending, forwarding and deletion; otherwise keep a manual write path.</p><h3>Add labels to the original messages first</h3><WorkflowPrompt id="gmail-labels" text={gmailPrompts.labels} title="Labels · Apply only to three confirmed originals"/><div class="wf-check"><b>Acceptance check</b><p>Corresponding GBG/ labels appear while old labels, inbox membership and read state remain. Record failures separately; a planned label is not an applied label.</p></div><h3>Review reply text before saving drafts</h3><p>Draft only where a reply is needed. For M08, Calendar has not been checked, so neither 10:00 nor 15:00 can be confirmed. Review the body before permitting a save.</p><WorkflowPrompt id="gmail-drafts" text={gmailPrompts.drafts} title="Drafts · Preview first, then save the approved scope"/><div class="wf-check"><b>Acceptance check</b><p>Open the actual draft and check recipient, original thread, tone and unknowns. Record original message_id and draft_id. Sent contains no new message. If tools cannot establish success, say saved state unverified.</p></div><p>Draft identity differs from the original message; a matching subject is not enough to detect duplicates. <a class="wf-source-ref" href={officialSources[6].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gmail draft reference ↗</a></p></section>
  <section id="repeat" class="wf-stage"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>STEP 05</span><h2 id="repeat-heading">Validate manually, save a Skill, then review a Routine</h2></div><p>Rerun the same small batch to check duplicate labels, duplicate drafts and partial failures. Save the accepted method only after reviewing outcomes. <a class="wf-source-ref" href={officialSources[1].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Skills and Routines reference ↗</a></p><WorkflowPrompt id="gmail-skill" text={gmailPrompts.skill} title="Reuse · Draft a manually accepted Skill"/><p>During the first week, one daily run in the current private conversation is easier to inspect. Retain the specifically authorized label/draft scope. After any approved creation, verify frequency, time zone and next run time.</p><WorkflowPrompt id="gmail-routine" text={gmailPrompts.routine} title="Schedule · Review a Routine proposal first"/><div class="wf-check"><b>Acceptance check</b><p>One original does not create duplicate drafts, while a new reply in the same thread is still inspected. Explain limits, pagination, retries and partial success. Stable tools and persistent state are required; without them, continue manually.</p></div></section>
  <section id="troubleshoot"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>DAILY USE</span><h2 id="troubleshoot-heading">Locate problems from the evidence</h2></div><div class="wf-faq">{problems.map(([title,body])=><details><summary>{title}</summary><p>{body}</p></details>)}</div><h3>Acceptance checklist for the first complete trial</h3><p>These page-local checks do not connect Gmail or create tasks and reset on refresh.</p><fieldset class="wf-checklist"><legend class="wf-sr-only">Email workflow acceptance</legend>{checks.map(check=><label><input type="checkbox" data-wf-check/><span>{check}</span></label>)}</fieldset><p class="wf-check-progress" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-wf-check-progress>Checked 0 / {checks.length} items</p></section>
  <section id="downloads"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>PRACTICE MATERIALS</span><h2 id="downloads-heading">Give these files directly to a Bot</h2></div><p>Start with input and rules, then inspect references. All files are generated by this site without real messages, credentials or external attachments.</p><div class="wf-downloads">{[['source-mails.json','Original synthetic emails','8 inputs without classification answers'],['label-rules.md','Label rules','6 business labels plus Review'],['expected-results.csv','Reference classification','Labels, evidence and next steps'],['daily-digest.txt','Example daily brief','Format and exceptions'],['practice-prompts.txt','All page prompts','7 staged instructions']].map(([file,title,description])=><a href={`${gmailGuideUrl}files/${file}`} download={file}><span><strong>{title}</strong><small>{file} · {description}</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">↓</b></a>)}</div></section>
  <section id="sources"><div class="wf-section-title"><span>SOURCES & SCOPE</span><h2 id="sources-heading">What has evidence, and what still needs validation</h2></div><CaseVerification slug="gmail-inbox-triage" english /><ul class="wf-source-list">{officialSources.map(source=><li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.title} ↗</a><p>{source.note}</p></li>)}</ul></section>
  <div class="wf-guide-end"><p>Use the same evidence-first method for meeting preparation,documents and conversations.</p><a href={officeBase} class="wf-button">Return to Office & information →</a></div>
 </article><aside class="wf-toc" data-pagefind-ignore aria-label="On this page"><div class="wf-kicker">ON THIS PAGE</div><ol>{toc.map(([id,title])=><li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}</ol><a href={officeBase} class="wf-toc-back">← Back to office topic</a></aside></div>
</div>
<script>
 const checks=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-wf-check]')];const update=()=>{const progress=document.querySelector('[data-wf-check-progress]');if(progress)progress.textContent=`Checked ${checks.filter(check=>check.checked).length} / ${checks.length} items`;};checks.forEach(check=>check.addEventListener('change',update));
</script>
